        <briefdescription>
<para>Calculate the cross section of the hard body at a given state. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The hard body is projected along the Z axis of the given frame onto its X-Y plane. Only the frame orientation is used: the cross section is always relative to the object position. Use the encounter frame (see <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1conjunction_1_1_close_approach_1a9fc81b80bd44e79e1f4b8334b3bb39fa" kindref="member">CloseApproach::computeEncounterFrame</ref>, whose Z axis is the relative velocity) to project onto the encounter plane.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">Shared&lt;const<sp/>Frame&gt;<sp/>encounterFrame<sp/>=<sp/>closeApproach.computeEncounterFrame()<sp/>;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">HardBody::CrossSection<sp/>crossSection<sp/>=<sp/>hardBody.calculateCrossSectionAt(state,<sp/>encounterFrame)<sp/>;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aState</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A state of the object </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aFrameSPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A frame whose axes define the projection </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The cross section </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
